WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:01.134
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.949
- My gosh.
(indistinct)

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:03.990
I know, you look so good.

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.263
Have y'all ever met?

00:00:05.263 --> 00:00:06.096
- We have not.
- Okay.

00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:06.929
- No we haven't.

00:00:06.929 --> 00:00:07.762
- But what an honor.

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:08.910
- I'm like, Jesus, just
bringing people together.

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.250
Okay, so, so I have to ask you.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.870
This is the craziest story to me.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.370
So you are from Atlanta?

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:15.441
- I am, born and raised.

00:00:15.441 --> 00:00:20.130
- And then you're in a, where,
where does the jump to go

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.750
to Korean competition show?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.980
Where, what happened there?

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:23.813
- This is a story.
- Okay.

00:00:23.813 --> 00:00:27.600
- Okay, so go to school,
graduate, get a job

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.110
at Deloitte Consulting doing
strategy, ask for a year off.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.010
And I went to India to do
service work, essentially.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:37.500
And while I was there, I got a email

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.680
through a YouTube video
that a TV show I'd watched.

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.210
And I thought it was a scam.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.407
And it said like, "Hey, come to Korea.

00:00:44.407 --> 00:00:45.510
"Send us your passport."

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.470
What happens when you do that?

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.140
You lose your identity.
- Send us your passport.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.760
- Yes and I was like, this is gonna,

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.560
this is a scam.
- This is shady.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.100
- But I was like I've always
wanted to do a music thing.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.410
Why not just send just enough information

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.090
to see if they send me a flight?

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.410
And sure enough, they did.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.149
So I get to Korea a few days later.

00:01:04.149 --> 00:01:07.320
Started an audition program
very much like the one

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.197
you were on.
- Yeah.

00:01:08.197 --> 00:01:11.130
- And then I got to the top
five, signed a record deal,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.090
quit my job, and started
my career in music.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.254
- Yeah, what a story.
(audience applauding)

00:01:18.254 --> 00:01:19.623
To grow up in Atlanta.

00:01:19.623 --> 00:01:22.380
And I just thought that was a crazy jump.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.570
So, I hear they have a
nickname for you in Korea.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.990
(Eric laughing)
I love this nickname.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.543
Did you love it?

00:01:29.543 --> 00:01:31.860
- It was, it was.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.390
- The nation's boyfriend?
- Yeah.

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.984
I was like, do I say this myself?

00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:35.817
- Nation's?

00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:37.890
It's, I think it's, is it
the Nation's boyfriend?

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.540
- Yeah, I was called
the Nation's boyfriend.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.400
- That's just like everyone's boyfriend.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.303
I'm just, yeah.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.570
The nation's boyfriend,
what does this mean?

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.250
Have you asked?

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.020
- I was told, so pretty much

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.137
in Korea there's a phrase
called (speaking in Korean).

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.170
So that means one Eric Nam per household.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:58.428
So it's like.
(audience laughing)

00:01:58.428 --> 00:02:01.530
It's like actually kind of
in like the dictionaries

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.363
and like if you search
it, it's like a thing.

00:02:02.363 --> 00:02:04.740
- Oh, you're like Beyonce
with Bootylicious.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.480
You just like made a word.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.350
Like that's incredible.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:08.430
- But here's the thing, I didn't make it.

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:10.800
I don't know who made it, but it was made

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.420
and then all of a sudden I
was on this fun reality show.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:18.810
It was, you know, reality
where I'm fake married

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.130
for like nine months.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.680
And through that and
through being on all these.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.849
I know, I know, I know.

00:02:23.849 --> 00:02:24.682
I know, I know.
- How did you like

00:02:24.682 --> 00:02:25.680
being married?

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:26.816
How did you like being married?

00:02:26.816 --> 00:02:27.649
- It was great.

00:02:27.649 --> 00:02:28.624
- It doesn't stick for everyone.

00:02:28.624 --> 00:02:29.670
(both laughing)

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.020
- Well, mine was like nine months.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:31.853
- Okay.

00:02:31.853 --> 00:02:32.872
- You know, again, it was -
- Some are, yeah.

00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:35.430
- It was a.
- In reality

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:36.750
- Also true.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.583
- But it was fun.

00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:38.430
But it was through doing a lot

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:43.050
of shows and I was on any
sort of TV show, radio show

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.040
anything, everywhere.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.530
And I think people just
really saw me everywhere.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.140
And I think people liked me in general.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:49.973
And so I got

00:02:49.973 --> 00:02:50.910
that name.
- You're very likable.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:52.936
- Thank you so much.
- Yes, you are very likable.

00:02:52.936 --> 00:02:53.769
- Thank you so much.

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:54.602
- So "House on a Hill".

00:02:54.602 --> 00:02:57.240
Where did this album title come from?

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.620
- I was wanting to buy a house

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.580
and I was looking all around.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.830
I happened to find this
beautiful house in LA

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.320
and I was like, "This is the home."

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.237
And then I was like, "Wait,
but I'm never anywhere.

00:03:07.237 --> 00:03:08.940
"Do I really need?"
- Yeah.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:09.773
- To make this thing?

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:10.800
And then I thought of,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.720
I went down this rabbit hole of thinking

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.060
about all the things that
we're told we need to be happy

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:15.930
or successful.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.690
That is getting property
or having a certain family

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.894
or looking a certain way
or having all these things.

00:03:20.894 --> 00:03:21.930
- You think if I do this, I'll be happy.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.190
If I have this, yeah.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:24.780
- But then I started to realize it's like

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.670
no matter what you have
you're always gonna

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.250
want the shiniest, the newest thing.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.070
The upgrade and -
- Apple gets us every time.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.630
- Every time they get us, right.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.497
- It's the same damn phone.
- I don't stand

00:03:34.497 --> 00:03:37.188
in line anymore though.

00:03:37.188 --> 00:03:38.206
I'm not standing in line no more.

00:03:38.206 --> 00:03:39.039
- I'm not standing in line.

00:03:39.039 --> 00:03:40.110
- I'll order it on the.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.490
- Yeah, wait til they work

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.630
out the kinks.
- Yes.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:43.463
- You're right though.

00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:45.540
That is true, like,
especially when we're younger.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.960
We think like, "Oh, this
will make me happy."

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.940
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.940
So that was kind of the
start of the process

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:52.830
which led me down a complete rabbit hole

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.020
of a existential crisis of sorts.

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.460
So just figuring out what makes me happy,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.530
what makes me tick, what
makes me really wanna get

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.720
up every day and do what I do.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.670
And that's kind of how
we built out the album,

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.560
trying to figure out some of those.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.180
- So that house on a hill
you thought you wanted

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.380
wasn't really what you wanted?

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.450
Yeah.
- No, I think one day I do,

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.283
but right now I'm good.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.690
I think it's enjoying
the process of creating,

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.300
of touring and meeting incredible
people like yourselves.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.830
- Yeah.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.120
Did you have that when you were younger?

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.140
I used to do that too.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:20.640
Especially 'cause I grew up with no money.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:21.787
Then they give you money and you're like,

00:04:21.787 --> 00:04:22.710
"What do I do with this?"

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.950
And I would you, totally
end up buying stuff.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:27.877
Like, "Oh, if I had this
house I've got in Texas.

00:04:27.877 --> 00:04:28.920
"If I did this."

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.600
I definitely went through all of that.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.560
Was not as smart as you.

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.873
Actually bought the house.

00:04:32.873 --> 00:04:35.599
And just, you know, kind of
went through the motions.

00:04:35.599 --> 00:04:36.510
Did you do that?

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.343
- I did, I did.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.780
You know, because the American dream says

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.110
that you're supposed to,
you know, have a house

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.647
and 2.3 kids and, you know.

00:04:45.647 --> 00:04:47.820
But I, and I felt bad about myself

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:50.490
for a long time 'cause I
was not a, I'm an artist.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.323
- Yeah.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:52.950
- You know, that's hand to
mouth, that's check to check.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:55.890
So like I didn't amass enough funds

00:04:55.890 --> 00:05:00.803
until I was 50 to buy
my first house, yeah.

00:05:02.916 --> 00:05:04.080
- You have enough experience
in that, I think you probably

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.940
made way better decisions than I did.

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:06.957
- Well, I don't know about that.

00:05:06.957 --> 00:05:10.170
'Cause I'm not really
that great with money so.

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.210
- It's important though
because society does tell you

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:14.430
like this is what you need to be happy.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.000
This is what you need.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:16.860
And everyone's different.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:20.700
So I, yeah, you're very clever
and smart to be so young.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.740
But we need to do another
commercial break, everybody.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:26.160
Eric's tour and album and song
are called "House on a Hill".

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.903
You can find both online.

